From: Robert Marko <robimarko@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:11:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: complete CPU frequency and cooling resources

Now that CPU clock is exposed and can be controlled, add the necessary
properties to the CPU nodes.

Since there is CPU Freq support as well as thermal sensor support now for
the IPQ8074, add cooling cells to CPU nodes so that they can be used as
cooling devices using CPU Freq.

Add the QFPROM node and CPR fuses.

Now that there is NVMEM CPUFreq support for IPQ8074, we can add the OPP
table for SoC.

Adjust the supported hardware mask in the IPQ6018 CPU operating point table
so the described operating points are available to the platform.

Keep the final implementation of this responsibility directly; subsequent
repairs listed below are integrated without intermediate replacements.

Merged from:
  0122-arm64-dts-qcom-cpu-frequency-resources.patch - arm64: dts: qcom: complete CPU frequency and cooling resources
  0912-arm64-dts-qcom-ipq5018-remove-800MHz-OPP.patch - arm64: dts: qcom: ipq5018: remove the 800 MHz OPP

